    "badgeColor": "border-amber-500/60 bg-amber-950/80 text-amber-300",
    "title": {
      "en": "Cooldown Manager Now Available in WoW: Forever Beta",
      "es": "Cooldown Manager ya está disponible en WoW: Forever Beta"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Cooldown Manager Now Available in WoW: Forever Beta...",
      "es": "Cooldown Manager ya está disponible en WoW: Forever Beta..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6ab6a08a07f580.07986382\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">The Cooldown Manager from Retail is now available for testing in the WoW: Forever Beta.<br><br>The Cooldown Manager was originally added in Patch 12.0 with the <i>Midnight</i> expansion as a result of the addon disarmament. As WoW: Forever <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/wow-forever-will-have-addon-changes-from-midnight-382921\" data-contiguous=\"true\">has the same addon restrictions</a> and the same client as Retail, the Cooldown Manager can be ported over to Forever as well. In the second WoW: Forever Beta build, the Cooldown Manager is available for testing for Druids, Mages, Priests, Warriors, and Warlocks. <br><br>To turn on the Cooldown Manager, players need to go to Options -&gt; Advanced Options and then enable the Cooldown Manager. Once it's enabled, you can go to Edit Mode to move the location of tracked spells, and type /<wbr>cdm to edit which spells are shown. <br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1303177.jpg\" id=\"1303177\"><img height=\"500\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1303177.jpg?maxHeight=500\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image\" alt=\"CDM 1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\"></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1303178.jpg\" id=\"1303178\"><img height=\"500\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1303178.jpg?maxHeight=500\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image\" alt=\"CDM 2\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\"></a>&nbsp;</div><div class=\"quote-box exclude-units last\" data-type=\"blizzard\" data-has-links=\"true\" data-has-source=\"true\" data-has-toggle=\"true\"><div class=\"quote-source\">Blizzard</div><div class=\"quote-header\"><a href=\"https://us.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/2360696/1\" target=\"_blank\">View Original</a><a class=\"quote-toggle\" href=\"javascript:\" aria-label=\"Toggle quote visibility\"></a></div><div class=\"quote-body\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\"><ul class=\"first last\"><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\"><b>Cooldown Manager</b><ul class=\"last\"><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">The Cooldown Manager in World of Warcraft: Forever is intended to enhance gameplay by pulling critical information from the buff bar or action bar and placing it in a fully customizable location. By default, the Cooldown Manager is disabled, and it can be enabled in Options under the Gameplay Enhancement settings.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Druid, Mage, Priest, Warrior, and Warlock are available for testing the Cooldown Manager.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Additional classes will become testable in future updates.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">The most desired feedback for this feature is currently: spells that you wish were tracked by default.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">The Cooldown Manager does not yet support spell ranks. This will be resolved in a future Beta update.</div></li></ul></div></li></ul></div></div></div>\n            \n            <noscript>The Cooldown Manager from Retail is now available for testing in the WoW: Forever Beta.<br /><br />The Cooldown Manager was originally added in Patch 12.0 with the <i>Midnight</i> expansion as a result of the addon disarmament. As WoW: Forever <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/wow-forever-will-have-addon-changes-from-midnight-382921\">has the same addon restrictions</a> and the same client as Retail, the Cooldown Manager can be ported over to Forever as well. In the second WoW: Forever Beta build, the Cooldown Manager is available for testing for Druids, Mages, Priests, Warriors, and Warlocks. <br /><br />To turn on the Cooldown Manager, players need to go to Options -&gt; Advanced Options and then enable the Cooldown Manager. Once it's enabled, you can go to Edit Mode to move the location of tracked spells, and type /cdm to edit which spells are shown. <br /><br /><div class=\"quote-box\" data-type=\"blizzard\"><div class=\"quote-header\"></div><div class=\"quote-body\"><br /><br /><ul><li><b>Cooldown Manager</b><br /><br /> The Cooldown Manager in World of Warcraft: Forever is intended to enhance gameplay by pulling critical information from the buff bar or action bar and placing it in a fully customizable location. By default, the Cooldown Manager is disabled, and it can be enabled in Options under the Gameplay Enhancement settings.</li><li>Druid, Mage, Priest, Warrior, and Warlock are available for testing the Cooldown Manager.</li><li>Additional classes will become testable in future updates.</li><li>The most desired feedback for this feature is currently: spells that you wish were tracked by default.</li><li>The Cooldown Manager does not yet support spell ranks. This will be resolved in a future Beta update.</li></ul></div></div></noscript>            \n        ",
